# Run Away Together {1}{U}: "Choose two target creatures controlled by different players. Return those creatures to their owners' hands" (CR 115.1, 400.3).
# On turn 3 two Ornithopters of Bot1 are refused as the pair (the same controller, though two creatures), and an Ornithopter with Bot2's Forest (not a creature)
# is refused; Bot1's Ornithopter with Bot2's Elvish Mystic is taken, and each goes to its own owner's hand while the other Ornithopter stays. Mox Sapphire
# and an Island pay exactly {1}{U}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Run Away Together
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Run Away Together.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#1; Ornithopter#2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Forest)
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#1; Elvish Mystic)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Ornithopter
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Mox Sapphire; Island
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
